[center][size=6][b]NV Reactive Ragdoll[/b][/size]
[size=3]Physics-driven hit reactions for living NPCs - an xNVSE plugin[/size][/center]

[color=#ff9900][b]ALPHA 0.8.0 - public test build. Please send your NVReactiveRagdoll.log with any report.[/b][/color]

[size=4][b]What it does[/b][/size]
Euphoria-style deaths for New Vegas. Living NPCs fight exactly like in the vanilla game; when they die, their Havok ragdoll is driven by "muscles" instead of collapsing like a sack. Inspired by recent physics mods for Skyrim (Delirium, Precision, PLANCK) and by MadAce's Ragdolls for New Vegas, which it replaces.

[list]
[*][b]Dying on their feet[/b] - over-the-top, Euphoria-style: almost every death, headshots included, starts with the NPC fighting to stay up. Its legs really push against the ground to carry it, it holds its ground against small pushes and takes steps to catch itself when the bullet or its own momentum throws it off (capture-point stepping), windmilling its arms, looking at its shooter, clutching the wound. Extra bullets matter: a leg shot makes that leg give way, an arm shot leaves the arm hanging, a body shot folds it for a moment. It goes down when it truly loses its balance or runs out of strength, not on a timer.
[*][b]Falling[/b] - joints tense up and hands reach out to break the fall, then it writhes on the ground for a few seconds.
[*][b]Fire[/b] - burning NPCs die beating at the flames and kicking. [b]Electricity[/b] - they die shaking. [b]Explosions[/b] - thrown bodies windmill their arms and pedal in the air, then reach out to land. Detected from the weapon's damage type and projectile: weapons from other mods work without patches.
[*][b]Creatures[/b] - same deaths on their own skeletons.
[/list]
[b]Optional living reactions[/b] (off by default, one switch in the menu): flinch at the impact point, stagger and knockdown from a per-NPC hit "charge", burning and shocked NPCs flailing.

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Fallout: New Vegas 1.4.0.525 (TTW should work: same game executable, not tested yet)
[*][url=https://github.com/xNVSE/NVSE/releases]xNVSE[/url] 6.1 or newer
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/newvegas/mods/68776]NV Compatibility Skeleton[/url] (load it last among skeleton mods)
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
Install with your mod manager. Disable [b]Ragdolls[/b] (this mod replaces it). No plugin file, nothing to put in the load order.

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Ragdolls[/b] - do not use together (double death reactions). The log warns you if it is active.
[*][b]Explosion Reactions[/b] - detected: living NPCs hit by an explosion are left to its animations (configurable).
[*][b]Awesome / Dramatic Staggering[/b] - fine: they replace the game's hit animations, this mod adds physics on top.
[*]Other stagger mods - if NPCs stagger twice, set bStagger=0.
[*]Creatures - all of them react, on their own skeleton: no list to maintain, creature mods work too. Bigger creatures need harder hits to stagger or fall. Vanilla creature ragdolls are used (no retuned creature skeletons yet).
[/list]

[size=4][b]Settings[/b][/size]
In game: pause menu, Mod Configuration, [b]NV Reactive Ragdoll[/b] (10 pages, 105 options; needs [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/newvegas/mods/42507]MCM[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/newvegas/mods/93642]MCM Extender[/url], no plugin file). Changes apply when you close the pause menu.
Or edit Data\Config\NVReactiveRagdoll.ini, re-read as soon as it changes. Every reaction can be tuned or turned off. Debug keys: F8 lists the physics bodies of the NPC under the crosshair, F7 pushes it.

[size=4][b]Source and credits[/b][/size]
GPL-3.0, source on [url=https://github.com/XENOR31-Toulouse/FNV-RAGDOLL-FESTIVAL]GitHub[/url].
Game structure offsets from [b]JIP LN NVSE[/b] (jazzisparis, GPL-3) and [b]xNVSE[/b]. Design ideas from [b]Skyrim Delirium[/b] (GPL-3), [b]Precision[/b], [b]PLANCK[/b] and [b]Ragdolls[/b] by MadAce.

[size=4][b]Français[/b][/size]
Réactions physiques des PNJ vivants aux coups : ils tressaillent, titubent, tombent, se protègent en tombant, portent la main à leur blessure, battent des bras dans le feu, tremblent électrocutés. Remplace le mod Ragdolls. Nécessite xNVSE et NV Compatibility Skeleton. Réglages dans NVReactiveRagdoll.ini.
